    "summary": "SVG rejection bypass in Next.js image optimization",
    "description": "<!-- https://linear.app/vercel/issue/NSEC-438 -->\r\nOn self-hosted deployments, the Next.js image optimizer (`/_next/image`) can be made to process an attacker-supplied SVG even when SVG support is disabled with `dangerouslyAllowSVG: false` (the default). This reaches an SVG parser the application intended to keep disabled, increasing exposure to denial of service and SVG decoder vulnerabilities.",
